Z||000013||Jefrysuko||11-30-2001||01:59 AM||||So I guess you can teach a old Monkey new tricks.<P>Glad you were able to figure out your problem MM.||||reg||1
Z||000014||StuGood||11-30-2001||10:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodrv6:<BR><B>Maybe the magnet in the motor got turned around?  I did that once and the motor operated up only...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Wow! You guys   just taught me something new (no small feat).<BR>When I modified a couple of "old style" HL motors to work with the "new style" control module a long time ago, the darn things worked backwards!  Turn them on, they'd go down.  Turn 'em off, they popped up!  What on earth?!<P>I finally gave up and just switched polarity on the connectors going to the modified motors.  After that, they worked fine.  Guess what I bet I did when I had the motors apart  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ??<P>Rodrv6, thanks a million.  Glad you were able to "field" that question  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>   <P>||||reg||10
